  "configuration_id": "config_031",
  "reason": "Evidence: The best RNA-only configuration (scvi_n200, multiprofile, avgpool/transformer) achieves ~0.650-0.653 accuracy, while the only multimodal test (config_030: scvi_n200, multiprofile, resnet50, avgpool, concat) scored 0.632, slightly below RNA-only. Image-only models are very weak (0.21-0.23), raising the question of whether the image modality is fundamentally unhelpful or whether the concat fusion is simply the wrong strategy. Question: config_031 is identical to config_030 except it uses weighted fusion instead of concat, providing a clean single-variable comparison. If weighted fusion recovers or exceeds the RNA-only baseline (~0.650), it shows that fusion strategy is critical and multimodal is a viable direction worth further exploration. If it also underperforms, it strongly indicates the image modality (at least resnet50) is not contributing useful signal, allowing us to redirect budget toward RNA-only refinement. Why best under limited budget: This is the highest-information next step because it directly resolves the key uncertainty (is multimodal salvageable with better fusion?) with a minimal, controlled change, and the answer will determine whether subsequent experiments should target multimodal variants or focus on RNA-only optimization."
}

